From: XDial maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] magicsock,ipnlocal: add bounded HomeDERP reselection

An old peer can retain a live DERP route which no longer matches control's
cached node snapshot. Rotating the discovery key does not repair that state:
the peer may consume the full update and still later apply a stale DERPHome
mutation to its live endpoint.

Add one narrow Prepare-only recovery primitive. It selects the lowest-latency
measured alternate region, connects it as an auxiliary DERP, waits for the
current connection generation to receive ServerInfo, promotes it atomically as
the home until explicit lifecycle invalidation or magicsock close, and publishes
matching NetInfo. The LocalBackend wrapper commits only while the same control
client, node identity, and current-generation NetInfo baseline remain current.
It binds that NetInfo to a payload-free receipt. The receipt becomes accepted
only when a lite map HTTP request actually snapshots the same NetInfo revision
and PreferredDERP and receives a successful response. A later different
NetInfo is reported as superseded rather than mistaken for delivery. The
server-provided SelfNode HomeDERP remains diagnostic because the protocol has
no synchronous peer-consumption acknowledgement.

The operation does not expose region IDs outside the patched module and does
not claim peer recovery. A fresh WireGuard handshake and real-egress probe
remain the caller's only success criteria.

